  "family_quality_rules": [
    "Built dungeon pages need deliberate wall, floor, overhead, fixture, and depth design; stone blocks alone are not enough.",
    "Torches, sconces, grates, doors, traps, racks, and furnishings are premium coloring objects, not filler.",
    "Natural caves use geology rather than masonry and favor a few large formations.",
    "Trap pages must show cause-and-effect with large readable mechanisms.",
    "Use only a small subset of the library on one page; comprehensive library depth exists to create variety across many pages.",
    "Fixture anchoring must be literal: wall torches and wall sconces visibly attach to masonry with a bracket, ring, plate, or niche; they must not drift into freestanding floor lamps or posts."
  ],
